# ============================================================================
# TMLR submission (paper/): un-hide the paper source that *.tex / *.png / *.pdf hide.
!paper/**/*.tex
!paper/figures/*.png
!paper/figures/*.pdf
!paper/main.pdf

# The paper's data of record and its table/figure generators. Re-homed out of the
# gitignored archive/ tree on 2026-07-31: these are the only copies, and every
# number in the manuscript derives from them.
#
# ...and then the 2026-08 consolidation moved paper/ to docs/paper/. The data
# came with it; the SCRIPTS did not, and fell back into the gitignored archive/,
# so for eighteen days a clone of this repository could not regenerate a single
# table or figure. Both rules below were left pointing at a path that no longer
# exists. Re-homed a second time on 2026-08-19 to docs/paper/scripts/, which
# nothing under docs/ ignores -- these two lines are kept only as the record of
# how the copies were lost, and protect nothing.
!paper/data/**
!paper/scripts/**

# Track B / handoff documents and the working manuscript revision live in docs/
# and must not be hidden by the blanket *.tex / *.pdf rules above.
#
# 🛑 THESE TWO LINES DO NOT REACH `docs/archive/`, AND FOR WEEKS NOBODY KNEW.
# git never descends into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so a file-level negation can
# not re-include anything underneath one. `archive/` below is a bare pattern
# and therefore matches at ANY DEPTH, `docs/archive/` included -- so
# `docs/archive/MEETING_BRIEF.tex` and `.pdf`, the very files the comment above
# says are protected, were silently untracked. See the negation under it.
!docs/**/*.tex
!docs/**/*.pdf

# Hypothesis's library cache. `charmap.json.gz` (21 KB) was swept into the
# tracked set by 7f9181b3 and is a textbook committed build artifact:
# regenerable, machine-local, and never read by a human. Untracked
# 2026-09-10; the file stays on disk.
.hypothesis/

# Legacy / scratch trees: keep on disk, keep OUT of git
archive/
# 🛑 ...EXCEPT `docs/archive/`, WHICH IS THE PROJECT'S RECEIPT DRAWER AND MUST
# BE IN GIT. The house rule is "archive, don't delete", and until 2026-09-10
# archiving a file DID delete it: `git rm` from the old path, `mv` into
# `docs/archive/`, and the bare `archive/` above swallowed it. Thirteen files
# were sitting on one disk with no version history -- `main.tex` (150 KB),
# `PAPER_REVISION_TRACKER.md` (41 KB), `BLUE_REVISION_BRIEFING.md` (36 KB, while
# its OWN .tex and .pdf were tracked), `THESIS_CONTEXT.md`, `PAPER_PLAN.md`,
# `MISSING_EXPERIMENTS.md`, `NATIVE_RES_CAMPAIGN.md`, `PAPER_INDEX.md` and two
# result CSVs. Losing the tree would have lost them.
#
# This negation must name the DIRECTORY, not the files: re-including
# `docs/archive/**` alone still fails, because the parent is what is excluded.
# Build artifacts underneath are re-excluded by the *.aux / *.log rules below,
# which DO apply once the directory itself is visible again.
!docs/archive/
extra_experiments/
.agents/
skills-lock.json
logs/.hook_last_predictions_count

# LaTeX build artifacts (regenerable; final PDF is negated above)
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk

# Archived provenance + predictions (29 MB of tarballs). Kept on disk locally
